    fullDescription: "Flex is a Viennese nightlife institution, a legendary and defiantly gritty club burrowed into a tunnel beside the Danube Canal that has been at the heart of the city's underground and electronic music scene for decades. Its reputation rests above all on its sound: the main room is renowned for having one of the best and most powerful sound systems in Europe, making it a magnet for serious clubbers and a favoured stop for touring DJs and live acts across techno, house, drum and bass, indie, hip-hop and experimental electronica. The aesthetic is raw and unpretentious — concrete, graffiti, sweat and low light rather than glamour and bottle service — which is precisely the appeal for those who want substance over style. The programming is genuinely eclectic, with different nights catering to very different crowds, so it is worth checking who is playing before you go. Just as important is the setting outside the club: the canal-side terrace and café-bar in front of Flex is one of the most popular open-air hangouts in the city on warm evenings, where a young, mixed crowd gathers to drink cheaply, sit on the steps by the water and soak up the summer atmosphere long before the club fills up. Entry is affordable and the vibe inclusive and unpolished. For visitors wanting to experience Vienna's real, non-touristy nightlife — a proper late night of loud electronic music in an authentically grungy setting by the water — Flex remains the definitive choice, best approached late and with energy to spare.",
