    fullDescription: "Porgy & Bess is the beating heart of Vienna's jazz scene and one of the most respected jazz clubs in Europe, a serious, professionally run venue in the old town that presents an ambitious, high-quality programme of live music almost every night of the year. Housed in a former adult cinema cleverly converted into a proper concert club with tiered seating, good sightlines, excellent acoustics and a full bar, it manages to feel both intimate and grown-up, focused squarely on the music rather than being a place to chat over a background soundtrack. The bookings are genuinely impressive and wide-ranging: alongside the best of the Austrian and Central European jazz scene, it regularly attracts touring international stars and rising talents across the whole spectrum of the genre — straight-ahead and modern jazz, avant-garde and free improvisation, world music, funk, soul and cross-over projects — making it a favourite of both dedicated aficionados and curious newcomers. The atmosphere is attentive and appreciative, the kind of room where audiences actually listen, and the standard of musicianship is consistently high. Because it is a ticketed concert venue with a nightly changing bill, it is well worth checking the programme in advance and booking ahead for popular acts, and arriving early helps secure a better spot. Centrally located and easy to reach, it offers a completely different, more cultured flavour of Viennese nightlife than the clubs and bars. For anyone who loves live jazz, or simply wants a memorable evening of top-class music in an atmospheric setting, Porgy & Bess is an essential stop.",
