    fullDescription: "Jazzland is the oldest jazz club in Vienna and a wonderfully atmospheric counterpoint to the modern Porgy & Bess, a cosy, characterful venue that has been keeping traditional jazz alive since 1972 in one of the most evocative settings imaginable. It occupies a series of ancient vaulted brick cellars said to date back to the twelfth century, tucked beneath street level beside the tiny Ruprechtskirche — Vienna's oldest church — in the old 'Bermuda Triangle' nightlife quarter near the canal. Descending the stairs into the warm, low, candlelit stone vaults, drink in hand, to hear live music in a space that has stood for 800 years is an experience in itself, intimate and timeless. Musically, Jazzland stays true to its roots, specialising in the classic, foot-tapping end of the spectrum — New Orleans and Dixieland, swing, blues, boogie-woogie and mainstream traditional jazz — performed by dedicated Austrian and visiting musicians for an appreciative, often loyal regular audience, with the option of simple Viennese food to accompany the show. It is smaller, more old-fashioned and more purely traditional in focus than the eclectic Porgy & Bess, and that is exactly its charm: this is jazz as a warm, convivial, unpretentious cellar tradition rather than a slick concert. Concerts run on set evenings, so check the schedule and consider booking, especially at weekends, and arrive in good time to get a table close to the band in the atmospheric vaults. For lovers of classic jazz and anyone seeking a magical, historic and genuinely local night out, Jazzland is a Viennese treasure.",
