    fullDescription: "The Dachboden ('attic') is the rooftop bar of the 25hours Hotel beside the MuseumsQuartier, and it has become one of the most popular and enjoyable spots in Vienna for a drink with a view, especially at golden hour. Perched on top of the playful design hotel, it combines a laid-back, boho-industrial interior of vintage furniture, rugs, plants and quirky bric-a-brac with an open-air terrace that delivers a genuinely lovely panorama over the rooftops of the 7th and 8th districts towards the neo-Gothic spires of the Rathaus, the greenery of the Ring and the hills beyond — a view that is at its most magical as the sun goes down over the city. The vibe is young, creative and relaxed rather than exclusive or stuffy, drawing a mix of hotel guests, local hipsters, after-work crowds and visitors, and it works equally well for an afternoon coffee, a sunset aperitivo or a longer cocktail-fuelled evening. The drinks list runs to well-made cocktails, spritzes, wine and beer, with some sharing plates and snacks to accompany them, and DJs often add to the atmosphere later on. Because the view and the setting are such a draw, it gets busy on warm evenings and there is no reservation for the terrace, so the trick is to arrive early — ideally before sunset — to bag an outdoor table. Its location right by the MuseumsQuartier and the Ring museums makes it an easy and rewarding stop to round off a day's sightseeing or begin a night out in the lively Neubau district. For rooftop views and a fun, unpretentious buzz, Dachboden is one of Vienna's best.",
