    fullDescription: "Julius Meinl am Graben is Vienna's most famous and prestigious gourmet food store, an institution founded in 1862 whose distinctive logo — a young boy in a fez — is a familiar sight across Austria, and whose flagship on the corner of the Graben and Kohlmarkt is a paradise for food lovers and a superb source of high-quality, distinctly Viennese edible souvenirs. Spread over several floors, it is a beautifully presented emporium of fine food and drink from Austria and around the world: superb coffee (the company built its name as a coffee roaster and it remains central to the business), premium chocolates and pralines, Austrian wines and international vintages, cheeses, charcuterie, patisserie, preserves, teas, spices and gourmet specialities, much of it perfect for gifts and beautifully packaged. The store combines the hushed elegance of a luxury delicatessen with the practicality of a genuine grocer for the well-heeled residents of the inner city, and browsing its counters is a pleasure in itself. Upstairs, a stylish café, bar and restaurant with views over the Graben lets you sit down for excellent coffee, breakfast, lunch or a glass of wine surrounded by the wares, making it a refined stop during a day's sightseeing or shopping. Prices reflect the quality and the address, but for coffee, chocolate, wine and other authentic Austrian gourmet products to bring home — or simply to admire a piece of Viennese food heritage — Julius Meinl is the definitive choice, ideally located in the heart of the shopping district steps from Stephansdom and the Hofburg.",
